 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "구동사 get up / turn on / put on / look for",
   "en": "phrasal verbs: get up, turn on, put on, look for"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "구동사는 '동사 + 부사/전치사'가 합쳐져 새로운 뜻이 되는 표현입니다. get up(일어나다), turn on / off(켜다 / 끄다), put on / take off(입다 / 벗다), look for(찾다)처럼 하나의 덩어리로 외웁니다. 목적어가 대명사이면 turn it on처럼 동사와 부사 사이에 놓습니다.",
   "en": "A phrasal verb is a verb + particle that has its own meaning: get up, turn on / off, put on / take off, look for. Learn them as chunks. A pronoun object goes in the middle: turn it on, put it on."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "get up / sit down",
     "I get up at six. Please sit down."
    ],
    [
     "turn on / off",
     "Turn on the TV. Turn it off."
    ],
    [
     "put on / take off",
     "Put on your coat. Take off your shoes."
    ],
    [
     "look for",
     "I'm looking for my keys."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "구동사는 덩어리로 외웁니다.",
    "en": "Learn phrasal verbs as chunks."
   },
   {
    "ko": "대명사는 중간에: turn it on (turn on it ✗).",
    "en": "Pronouns go in the middle: turn it on (not turn on it)."
   },
   {
    "ko": "look for = 찾다 (진행형으로 자주 씁니다).",
    "en": "look for = search for (often used in the continuous)."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
   {
    "t": "I get up at six.",
    "ko": "나는 6시에 일어나요."
   },
   {
    "t": "Turn on the TV, please.",
    "ko": "TV 좀 켜 줘요."
   },
   {
    "t": "Turn off the light before you leave.",
    "ko": "나가기 전에 불을 꺼요."
   },
   {
    "t": "I'm looking for my keys.",
    "ko": "나는 열쇠를 찾고 있어요."
   },
   {
    "t": "Take off your shoes at home.",
    "ko": "집에서는 신발을 벗어요."
   }
  ],
